# librarian-bot
**I see you're talking about a librarian that progressively discovers wiki skills, bots, and loops — want a bot that surfaces them via progressive disclosure in the wiki rows?**

Progressive-disclosure bot that scans topic skills/bots/loops and renders front-matter summaries first, drilling to detail on demand

## First task
Implement front-matter-first rendering for the SKILLS section rows; click expands the summary card in-place

## SOUL.md (draft)
SOUL.md: name=librarian, trigger=watcher sees SKILLS/BOTS/LOOPS section render, behavior=read topics/*/skills/SKILL.md front-matter + proposed bot/loop files, emit rows with hollow ring + PROPOSED tag per approval-policy, drill-down via click-pin card (not a page) respecting one-page-navigation, live mdRender for baked READMEs.

## Evidence
> We can use progressive disclosure just like how skills are discovered by first through the font matter and then it could dig deeper
> We can have a librarian watching the whole thing and progressively discovering, wiki skills, bots, and loops
